    "specialInstructions": "Fill the citrate tube to its marked line. Follow the test-specific centrifugation and freezing instructions. Collection details: Centrifuge light blue-top tube for 15 minutes at approximately 1500 g within 60 minutes of collection. Using a plastic pipette, remove plasma, taking care to avoid the WBC/platelet buffy layer and place into a plastic vial. Centrifuge a second time and transfer platelet-poor plasma into a new plastic vial. Plasma must be free of platelets (<10,000/uL). Freeze immediately and ship on dry ice. Unacceptable specimens: Hemolysis • Received thawed",
